---
/* L22 - attention: query-key scores become a row of fractions that sums to one. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L22.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a square grid of small cells with the three cells in the top row shaded pale blue to solid dark blue, and beneath it three horizontal bars of different lengths with a small disc travelling along the top bar."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L22-fig-title L22-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L22-fig-title">From raw scores to a row of fractions that sums to one</title>
      <desc id="L22-fig-desc">
        Three steps left to right. First, a matrix of raw query-key scores whose
        cells are labelled with positive and negative numbers. Second, the same
        matrix after dividing by the square root of the key dimension, with the
        gap between the top score and the runner-up visibly narrowed. Third,
        the first row of the matrix after the softmax, holding the fractions
        0.2, 0.3 and 0.5, which sum to one, with the strongest cell shaded.
      </desc>

      <!-- step 1 -->
      <text x="24" y="32" class="fig-label">1 raw scores</text>
      <g class="fig-grid">
        <rect x="24" y="48" width="128" height="128" />
      </g>
      <g class="fig-cell fig-cell--neg">
        <rect x="24" y="48" width="42" height="42" />
        <rect x="67" y="91" width="42" height="42" />
      </g>
      <g class="fig-cell fig-cell--pos">
        <rect x="110" y="134" width="42" height="42" />
        <rect x="67" y="134" width="42" height="42" />
      </g>
      <text x="34" y="74" class="fig-text fig-text--num">-2</text>
      <text x="77" y="117" class="fig-text fig-text--num">-1</text>
      <text x="120" y="160" class="fig-text fig-text--num">6</text>
      <text x="77" y="160" class="fig-text fig-text--num">4</text>
      <text x="24" y="192" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">raw, can be negative</text>

      <!-- step 2 -->
      <text x="196" y="32" class="fig-label">2 scaled by 1/sqrt(d_k)</text>
      <g class="fig-grid">
        <rect x="196" y="48" width="128" height="128" />
      </g>
      <g class="fig-cell fig-cell--neg">
        <rect x="196" y="48" width="42" height="42" />
        <rect x="239" y="91" width="42" height="42" />
      </g>
      <g class="fig-cell fig-cell--pos">
        <rect x="282" y="134" width="42" height="42" />
        <rect x="239" y="134" width="42" height="42" />
      </g>
      <text x="206" y="74" class="fig-text fig-text--num">-1.0</text>
      <text x="249" y="117" class="fig-text fig-text--num">-0.5</text>
      <text x="292" y="160" class="fig-text fig-text--num">3.0</text>
      <text x="249" y="160" class="fig-text fig-text--num">2.0</text>
      <text x="196" y="192" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">gaps narrowed, still not fractions</text>

      <!-- step 3 -->
      <text x="368" y="32" class="fig-label">3 softmax, row-wise</text>
      <g class="fig-grid">
        <rect x="368" y="48" width="128" height="128" />
      </g>
      <g class="fig-cell fig-cell--weight-soft">
        <rect x="368" y="48" width="42" height="42" />
        <rect x="411" y="48" width="42" height="42" />
      </g>
      <g class="fig-cell fig-cell--weight">
        <rect x="454" y="48" width="42" height="42" />
      </g>
      <text x="376" y="74" class="fig-text fig-text--num">0.2</text>
      <text x="419" y="74" class="fig-text fig-text--num">0.3</text>
      <text x="462" y="74" class="fig-text fig-text--num">0.5</text>
      <text x="368" y="192" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--ink">row 0 sums to 1.0</text>

      <!-- the arrows between the steps -->
      <g class="fig-step-arrow">
        <path d="M158 112 H190" />
        <path d="M190 112 l-6 -3 v6 z" class="fig-step-head" />
        <path d="M330 112 H362" />
        <path d="M362 112 l-6 -3 v6 z" class="fig-step-head" />
      </g>

      <!-- row 0 read over the tokens -->
      <g>
        <rect x="24" y="212" width="472" height="94" class="fig-panel" />
        <text x="38" y="234" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">row 0 reads over the tokens</text>
        <text x="38" y="256" class="fig-text">the</text>
        <text x="150" y="256" class="fig-text">cat</text>
        <text x="250" y="256" class="fig-text">dog</text>
        <rect
          class="fig-bar fig-bar--weak"
          x="38" y="264" width="38" height="14"
          style="transform-origin: 38px 264px; animation-delay: 0s"
        />
        <rect
          class="fig-bar fig-bar--weak"
          x="150" y="264" width="56" height="14"
          style="transform-origin: 150px 264px; animation-delay: 0.15s"
        />
        <rect
          class="fig-bar fig-bar--strong"
          x="250" y="264" width="94" height="14"
          style="transform-origin: 250px 264px; animation-delay: 0.3s"
        />
        <text x="38" y="296" class="fig-text fig-text--num">0.2</text>
        <text x="150" y="296" class="fig-text fig-text--num">0.3</text>
        <text x="250" y="296" class="fig-text fig-text--num">0.5</text>
        <text x="360" y="296" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">the dog gets the most</text>
      </g>

      <!-- the scaling warning -->
      <g>
        <rect x="510" y="212" width="106" height="94" class="fig-panel fig-panel--ink" />
        <text x="522" y="234" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">without</text>
        <text x="522" y="250" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">the scale</text>
        <text x="522" y="274" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">one cell</text>
        <text x="522" y="290" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">takes it all</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L22</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">Raw query-key scores are scaled, then softmaxed row by row, so each reader ends up holding a set of fractions over the tokens that sums to one.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-text--ink {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text--dim {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text--num {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fig-grid rect {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-rule);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-cell rect {
    stroke: none;
  }

  .fig-cell--neg rect {
    fill: var(--color-ground-deep);
  }

  .fig-cell--pos rect {
    fill: var(--color-prussian-tint);
  }

  .fig-cell--weight rect {
    fill: var(--color-prussian);
  }

  .fig-cell--weight-soft rect {
    fill: var(--color-prussian-tint);
  }

  .fig-step-arrow path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-ink-45);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-step-arrow .fig-step-head {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
    stroke: none;
  }

  .fig-panel {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-rule-soft);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-panel--ink {
    stroke: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-bar {
    stroke: none;
  }

  .fig-bar--weak {
    fill: var(--color-prussian-tint);
  }

  .fig-bar--strong {
    fill: var(--color-prussian);
  }

  /* the one idea of motion: the attention row fills in as fractions */
  @keyframes l22-fill {
    from {
      transform: scaleX(0);
    }
    to {
      transform: scaleX(1);
    }
  }

  .fig-bar {
    animation: l22-fill 0.9s ease-out both;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .fig-bar {
      animation: none !important;
      transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
